To mitigate the risk of supply chain attacks and unauthorized script modifications, always use Subresource Integrity (SRI) when loading external resources. This ensures that the file being loaded has not been altered by malicious actors. Prefer self-hosting critical third-party scripts instead of relying on external CDNs to minimize risks.
