Finding 8
Weak TLS Certificate
Application initializes an SSL/TLS context using the generic "TLS" protocol identifier. This configuration does not explicitly restrict the connection to approved TLS protocol versions or specify secure cryptographic settings, potentially allowing weaker protocols or configurations depending on the JVM and runtime environment.
(Affected Source File/Line number: None specified)
If outdated or insecure TLS protocols or cipher suites are negotiated, communications may be vulnerable to cryptographic attacks, potentially compromising the confidentiality and integrity of transmitted data.
Low
Explicitly enforce TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.3, disable obsolete protocols and weak cipher suites, and ensure that the application uses the JVM's secure default trust store to validate server certificates. Verify the effective TLS configuration before classifying this finding as a confirmed vulnerability.
