Access Control is the application of constraints on who or what can perform attempted actions or access resources that they have requested. Access Control determines whether the user can carry out the action that they are attempting to perform.
The application's Technical resource functionality is vulnerable to authorization bypass in the Edit Resource details operation. An Asset manager user can capture or obtain a valid entity update request and replay it using their own authenticated session. The application processes the PUT request successfully and returns an HTTP 200 OK response without validating whether the user has edit privileges. As a result, an Asset Manager user is able to modify entity records that should only be managed by the Supporter role.
